# National BIG geodatabase (340 MB, manually downloaded, not redistributable here).
# Derive data/boundaries/ from it with scripts/extract_boundary.sh
*.gdb/
*.gdb.zip

# Himawari raw band-segments (~100 MB/day) and evening products - never
# commit; the producer is manual and closes on a different schedule (Task 08
# section 4).
data/raw/himawari/
data/processed/himawari_evening_*.parquet

# --- field survey ---
# Rebuilt from the tracked store by src/fieldwork_gpkg.py, so the targets are
# reproducible and need no commit. The survey layer is the reason this is a
# rule rather than tidiness: it fills with GPS positions and photographs of
# people's land, and no ethical clearance or consent procedure exists yet.
# Nothing from here goes near docs/.
fieldwork/

# --- reference material, not ours to redistribute ---
# NASA ARSET training slides and the Mandum Rimba white paper are third-party
# documents kept locally for reference. Cite them; do not republish them.
ARSET_NASA/
mandum_rimba/
mandum_rimba-*.zip
# Downloaded papers and product user guides (Alcaras et al. 2022 on NBR+,
# the MOD16 user guide). Cite them; the publishers hold the PDFs.
References/

# Boundaries for a different kabupaten, kept for unrelated work.
data/boundaries/yahukimo_desa.geojson

# Own published paper, kept for reference; the publisher holds the typeset PDF.
Analyisis_of_Drought_in_*.pdf

# --- local GeoLibre workspace ---
# The project file inlines its layers, so it grows to megabytes and carries
# whatever it is pointed at, including the fieldwork points that fieldwork/
# exists to keep out of the repository. It is a local inspection tool, not a
# deliverable: build it, look at it, and let it stay untracked.
*.geolibre
*.geolibre.json
# the GeoJSON the project is assembled from; inlined on the way in,
# so the folder is scratch and can be rebuilt at any time
geolibre_data/
